# Every setting Docker Compose reads. Copy what you need into .env, or run `make env` to
# create one with random values. Lines starting with # are optional and off.

# --- Required -------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The database password. The server refuses to start with this placeholder.
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=changeme

# Encrypts stored Google tokens, and the keys of files in encrypted folders. Back this up:
# without it, every linked account has to be connected again, and encrypted files can never
# be read, even with a database backup. The format is id:base64, for 32 random bytes:
#   k1:$(openssl rand -base64 32)
ENCRYPTION_KEYS=changeme

# Which key new values use. Only needed with several keys. To rotate, add a new key after a
# comma in ENCRYPTION_KEYS, point this at its id, and keep the old key listed.
# ENCRYPTION_KEY_ID=k2

# --- Google: needed to link Drive accounts, which is where files are stored --------------

# Both turn on Google sign-in and linking Drive accounts. In the Google Cloud console, enable
# the Drive API, add the drive.file scope, and add these authorized redirect URIs:
#   <PUBLIC_URL>/api/v1/auth/google/callback
#   <PUBLIC_URL>/api/v1/storage/google/callback
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Turns on Add from Drive. Enable the Google Picker API in the same project, and create an API
# key limited to that API. Its allowed sites must be the app's address and
# https://docs.google.com/*
# GOOGLE_PICKER_API_KEY=

# --- Address ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The address browsers use. Changing requests from anywhere else are refused, and Google's
# redirect URIs follow it. Defaults to http://127.0.0.1:3000.
# PUBLIC_URL=https://files.example.org

# --- HTTPS -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Runs nginx in front of the app, on https://127.0.0.1, which gives browsers HTTP/2 and so
# more uploads at once. Run `make cert` first, set PUBLIC_URL to match, and add the new
# address to Google's redirect URIs above.
# COMPOSE_PROFILES=https

# The address or range of a reverse proxy in front of the web service, so visitors' real
# addresses reach the rate limits and the audit log. The default is the nginx service above.
# TRUSTED_PROXIES=172.30.0.1

# --- Rarely needed ---------------------------------------------------------------------

# The port the app listens on, for the docker-compose.yml from the website only.
# PORT=3000

# The version a build reports. `make up` sets this from the VERSION file, so it's only for
# running plain `docker compose up --build` yourself.
# VERSION=0.1.3
